See the Pen [Table - scrollbars with background \[forked\]] by [Adrian Bece].

Notice how shadows subtly hide and show as we scroll from one edge to another.

[]

The shadow appears and disappears depending the direction where user can scroll. ([Large preview])

[]

On devices where scrollbars are hidden by default, the subtle shadow indicates that a table can be scrolled. ([Large preview])

Keep in mind that `background-attachment` property is [not supported on iOS Safari] and a few other browsers, so make sure to either **provide a fallback or remove the background on unsupported browsers**.

